{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462317-mind-s-eye-theatre-changeling-custom-printed-book","id":1462317,"title":"Mind's Eye Theatre: Changeling - Custom Printed Book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-01T13:27:26-07:00","id":1462317,"title":"Mind's Eye Theatre: Changeling - Custom Printed Book","content":"I was really sad when licensing issues meant that By Night Studios could only release their recent Mind's Eye Theatre Changeling book on the Storyteller's Vault. So I paid to have a custom version printed and bound and it came out looking really beautiful for a pretty affordable price! (About \u00a365). I used an online printing company that had hardcover book options, and facilities to upload and adjust/design covers, etc. I did some very minor editing to create the spine text from the cover lettering.<br /> <br /> I had to downscale the .pdf slightly as part of the process and it shows ever so slightly if you look closely at the cover, but the quality on the inner pages is extremely crisp. It's glue binding, not thread, so I am babying the spine a little. But for actual reading and use I can use my digital copy - this is mostly so it can take its rightful place on the my bookshelf alongside my other C:tD books.<br /> <br /> I don't think there are any legal concerns here but for the avoidance of doubt, I purchased the book from Storyteller's Vault and paid to have a single copy printed for my own personal use. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/T5G79S2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/brUPRpX.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/BFDREOp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/FxTH041.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T13:49:25-07:00","id":1462319,"title":"","content":"There is no legal concerns, if any could be brought up it would be for distribution, something you're not doing. What you do with your own copy of something is up to you as long as you don't distribute, that's why it is called <u>copy</u>right.<br /> <br /> And it is really beautiful, but I wouldn't go that far to have a book without a sturdy binding. That's me, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}